# The tier this folder is. scripts/package-audio.sh rewrites these two lines, and
# the Title above, once per tier it builds; the tree in the repository is the
# 128kbps master every shipped tier is transcoded from, so it describes itself as
# the high tier. Data/Sounds.lua reads these back at load time and reports them
# to ZoneLore, which is how two tiers installed side by side can be told apart.
## X-SpokenZones-Quality: high
## X-SpokenZones-Bitrate: 128

# The language this pack narrates, read back the same way. Spoken Zones loads that
# language's lore for the captions and offers the pack under it; the player picks
# which installed pack plays, so it can narrate a language the client is not in.
## X-SpokenZones-Language: enUS

# Defines the SpokenZonesAudioPacks registry entry that Spoken Zones reads. No dependency
# is declared in either direction: Spoken Zones reads its lore without narrating when
# no pack is present, and a pack is inert without it.
Data/Sounds.lua
